-- title:
--   Kernel of R → S/mathfrak m_S^k for flat local extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings, both local, and let $S$ be an $R$-algebra whose structure map $\mathrm{algebraMap}\colon R \to S$ is a local homomorphism (it pulls the maximal ideal of $S$ back into the maximal ideal of $R$) and makes $S$ a flat $R$-module. Assume the ideal of $S$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_R = \mathrm{maximalIdeal}\,R$ is exactly $\mathfrak m_S = \mathrm{maximalIdeal}\,S$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_R S = \mathfrak m_S$. Then for every natural number $k$, the kernel of the composite ring homomorphism $R \to S \to S/\mathfrak m_S^{\,k}$, obtained by following $\mathrm{algebraMap}$ with the quotient map modulo $\mathfrak m_S^{\,k}$, equals $\mathfrak m_R^{\,k}$. Equivalently, the preimage in $R$ of $\mathfrak m_S^{\,k}$ is $\mathfrak m_R^{\,k}$; in particular $R/\mathfrak m_R^{\,k}$ injects into $S/\mathfrak m_S^{\,k}$. No Noetherian hypothesis is imposed, and the case $k = 0$ is included, both sides then being the unit ideal.
--
--   This is the standard contraction statement for a flat local homomorphism inducing an isomorphism on residue fields up to the condition $\mathfrak m_R S = \mathfrak m_S$: the $\mathfrak m$-adic filtrations correspond, level by level. It is used in the construction of a ring isomorphism between the adic completions of $R$ and $S$ under flatness, surjectivity on residue fields and $\mathfrak m_R S = \mathfrak m_S$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_ker_quotient_mk_comp_algebraMap_eq_maximalIdeal_pow_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq.lean

